     "part_tier": null,
     "problem_md": "A mixture of salt solution and an insoluble solid is separated by …**P**… .\n\nThe insoluble solid that is collected is the …**Q**… .\n\nPure salt crystals are obtained from the separated salt solution by …**R**… of the water.\n\nWhich words complete gaps **P**, **Q** and **R**?\n\n|   | **P** | **Q** | **R** |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **A** | evaporation | filtrate | filtration |\n| **B** | evaporation | residue | filtration |\n| **C** | filtration | filtrate | evaporation |\n| **D** | filtration | residue | evaporation |",
     "solution_md": "**Final answer:** **The correct answer is D**\n\n- Filtration separates the insoluble solid from the salt solution\n- The insoluble solid collected on the filter paper is called the residue\n- Evaporation of the water from the filtrate (the salt solution that passed through the filter) leaves pure salt crystals behind\n\n**A** is incorrect because evaporation cannot separate an insoluble solid from a solution; filtration must be used first\n\n**B** is incorrect because evaporation cannot separate an insoluble solid from a solution; filtration must be used first\n\n**C** is incorrect because the insoluble solid collected is called the residue, not the filtrate",
